<section class="hero"><div><p class="eyebrow">KENNY WU · AI ENGINEER · SHENZHEN</p><h1>From AI capability<br>to <span class="blue">reliable delivery.</span></h1><p class="lead">I’m Kenny, an AI application and systems engineer.<br>I bring language, retrieval, and multimodal models into real workflows.</p><div class="links"><a class="primary" href="mailto:jdlow@live.cn">Let’s discuss your project <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a href="#delivery">Explore delivery work <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a></div></div><aside class="hero-aside"><img src="/assets/img/practices/walk.png" width="1254" height="1254" alt="Illustration of Kenny on a walk"><p>From research to engineering,<br>with room left for thought.</p><a href="/about/">About me ↗</a></aside></section>
<section class="delivery" id="delivery" aria-labelledby="delivery-title"><div class="section-head"><p class="label">01 / SELECTED DELIVERY</p><span class="caption">Professional work · Roles & outcomes</span></div><div class="case-grid"><div class="case-copy"><p class="case-role"><time datetime="2026">2026</time> · Technical lead</p><h2 id="delivery-title">AI comics generation</h2><p class="case-thesis">Beyond generation,<br>quality checks and recovery matter.</p><p>Connected script understanding, asset extraction, and storyboard generation. Led quality evaluation and acceptance criteria.</p><a href="/about/#experience" class="text-link">See responsibilities and outcomes ↗</a></div><div class="case-evidence"><div class="workflow"><div class="figure-head"><span class="label">From script to evaluated storyboards</span><span class="caption">Workflow diagram</span></div><ol class="flow"><li><span>01 / UNDERSTAND</span><strong>Understand scripts</strong><small>Identify characters and plot</small></li><li><span>02 / ORGANIZE</span><strong>Extract assets</strong><small>Organize characters and scenes</small></li><li><span>03 / GENERATE</span><strong>Generate shots</strong><small>Structured shot decomposition</small></li></ol><div class="quality-loop"><strong>Independent checks</strong><span>→</span><strong>Bounded correction</strong><span>→</span><strong>Acceptance</strong></div><p class="recovery">Runtime safeguards: circuit breaking · concurrency control · bounded recovery</p></div><div class="proof"><div><p class="proof-label">Issue rate · Fixed evaluation set</p><p class="big-number"><span class="before">≈18%</span><span class="metric-arrow">→</span>9.53%</p><p class="caption">Action overload & shot-scale issues · ≈47% relative reduction</p></div><div><p class="proof-label">One real-world run</p><p class="big-number">20 <small>episodes</small></p><p class="caption">Completed despite intermediate failures</p></div></div></div></div></section>
<section class="support-case" aria-labelledby="rag-title"><div><p class="label">2024 / RETRIEVAL & ANSWERING</p><h2 id="rag-title">Enterprise document Q&A</h2><p>Combined paragraph hierarchy, multi-path retrieval, and dynamic thresholds into a document Q&A workflow.</p><a class="text-link" href="/about/#enterprise">See this work ↗</a></div><div class="rag-flow" aria-label="Document retrieval and answering workflow"><span>Document structure</span><span aria-hidden="true">→</span><span>Multi-path retrieval</span><span aria-hidden="true">→</span><span>Answer evaluation</span></div><div class="rag-result"><strong>≈90%</strong><p>Internal tests<br>Recall and Q&A accuracy</p></div></section>
<section class="judgments" aria-labelledby="judgment-title"><div class="section-head"><div><p class="label">02 / ENGINEERING JUDGMENT</p><h2 id="judgment-title">How I move the work forward</h2></div><a href="/about/#questions">Questions I return to ↗</a></div><div class="judgment-grid"><article><span class="number">01</span><h3>Define what good means first.</h3><p>Turn quality concerns into measurable criteria. Use a fixed evaluation set to check whether changes help.</p></article><article><span class="number">02</span><h3>Build failure into the workflow.</h3><p>Make long tasks recoverable and bound correction costs, so one failure does not stall delivery.</p></article><article><span class="number">03</span><h3>Connect models to real work.</h3><p>Check the workflow from retrieval and generation to service orchestration, bringing results to acceptance.</p></article></div></section>
